   "en": "Anna answered: 'O you who are [dearer|5,6] to your sister than the light itself, will you waste your whole youth alone, grieving, and never know sweet children, or the rewards of love? Do you really think the dust and ashes [of the dead|23,26] care about that?",
   "en_marked": "[Anna|1] [answered|2]: '[O|3] you who are [dearer|5,6] to your [sister|7] than the [light|4] {itself|Not in the Latin. Added for emphasis: luce means life itself, so Dido is dearer to Anna than anything.}, [will you waste|11] your [whole|9] [youth|12] [alone|8], [grieving|10], [and never|13] [know|19] [sweet|14] [children|15], [or|17] the [rewards|18] of [love|16]? [Do you|24] {really|Not in the Latin. Added to bring out the scornful tone of Anna's question with credis.} [think|24] the [dust and ashes|21] [of the dead|23,26] [care about|25] [that|20]?",
